# THE FROZEN --no-cover REFERENCE for tests/spells/lodgen_ground_cover.sh check C1.
#
# What it is: the sha256 of the three chunk sheets of Sanctuary chunk
# Commonwealth.4.-20.24, baked with ground cover OFF. C1's claim is that with the
# feature off NOT ONE BYTE MOVES, and "not one byte moved" measured against a
# fresh bake of the build under test is a bake compared with itself. These three
# hashes are the other side of that comparison and they are meant to outlive the
# build that produced them: a later build that changes any of the three has
# changed the far terrain with the feature off, and C1 is where that shows up.
#
# WRITTEN 2026-09-16 by lane GENSMALL1 (director ROW C, after bungo lifted his
# hold on freezing it).
#
# The build it was taken from:
#   release/NifSkope.exe   22,300,160 bytes   2026-09-16 13:52:56
#   sha256 4ad6ee0c4c844600cf361149c6b00fcdb6aaeeebd8bfec2905f596912a692ee0
#
# Why that build and not the 12:49:19 one the director named as the fallback:
# it is the exe on disk, it is the one every gate in that lane's report ran on,
# and its stock bake is not lane-specific. Two independent measurements say so:
#   * lodgen_native_baseline.sh --check, same day: 25 files in the baseline, 25
#     baked, 0 differ, against a baseline frozen on the 2026-09-10 03:57:46 exe;
#   * resource_ext.sh leg 5: a stock bake of (-20,24) dim 4 under this exe and
#     under the pre-lane rung, cmp'd file for file, 0 of them differ.
# So these hashes are the fork's --no-cover output, not this build's.
#
# The stated precondition of the freeze, met on the same exe before it was
# written: tests/spells/lodgen_identity.sh RESULT PASS (2026-09-16 14:2x).
#
# The bake: the spell's own `plain` bake -- worldspace 3C, --terrain-region
# -20 24 -20 24, --dim 4, --no-cover, the ruled defaults otherwise. Each sheet is
# 174,888 bytes and the _data sheet is still DXT1, which C1 checks separately, so
# a re-freeze that quietly turned one of them into BC3 would be caught by size
# and fourCC before it ever reached these lines.
#
# TO RE-FREEZE (only when a ruling deliberately moves the far terrain, and say
# which ruling in this header): run the spell, take the three lines it prints
# above check C1, and replace the three below. Do not edit one line by hand.
#
